<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teisheba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teisheba was the storm and war god of Urartu, second in the state pantheon after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haldi">Haldi</a>. A form of the Hurrian storm god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teshub">Teshub</a>, he was often shown standing on a bull, and the fortress-city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karmir-blur">Teishebaini</a>, now Karmir Blur near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yerevan">Yerevan</a>, was named after him. His consort was the goddess Huba, the Hurrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebat">Hebat</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teisheba.jpg" alt="Teisheba" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: liveon001 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teisheba.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
